<article class="env-lemma" id="0BA9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BA9">Lemma <span data-tag="0BA9">28.10.4</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. Let $x \in X$. Then $x$ is a generic point of an irreducible component of $X$ if and only if $\dim (\mathcal{O}_{X, x}) = 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/02IZ" data-tag="02IZ">28.10.3</a> for example. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>